  "verbalization": "The compound (2S,3R,4R,5R,6S)-2-[(2R,3R,4S,5R,6R)-3,5-dihydroxy-2-[(1R,2S,4S,5'R,6R,7S,8R,9S,12S,13R,16S,18S,19S)-16-hydroxy-5',7,9,13-tetramethylspiro[5-oxapentacyclo[10.8.0.02,9.04,8.013,18]icosane-6,2'-oxane]-19-yl]oxy-6-methyloxan-4-yl]oxy-6-methyloxane-3,4,5-triol is implicated in the activation of Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for several kinases, including RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase and Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src. Additionally, the compound is linked to the target of (6Z,10E,14Z,18E)-2,6,10,15,19,23-hexamethyltetracosa-2,6,10,14,18,22-hexaene, which in turn targets Src. Furthermore, the compound is also associated with the target of trans-Norbixin, which also leads to Src activation. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may function as a potential activator or modulator of Src, depending on the specific molecular context. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a possible role in Src signaling, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated."
